{"file_name": "ranjeet_resume.pdf", "category": "data_science", "text": "Ranjeet Matade\nG m\n\nEDUCATION\n. KIT\u2019s College of Engineering Kolhapur, India\nBachelor of Technology \u2014 CSE (Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning) \u2014 GPA: 8.65 2022 \u2014 2026\n\nCourses:(Operating Systems, Data Structures, Analysis of Algorithms, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning,\nNetworking, Databases)\n\n. AnnaSaheb Dange Medical and IIT Academy Ishwarpur, India\n12th Grade \u2014 Percentage: 74 2021 \u2014 2022\n. Vidyaniketan English Medium School (Ishwarpur) Ishwarpur, India\n10th Grade \u2014 Percentage: 88 2019-2020\n\nSKILLS SUMMARY\n\ne Languages: Java, Python, SQL, C, JavaScript\n\ne Data Science and ML: Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-learn, Streamlit\n\ne Databases: MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite\n\nTools and Platforms: Git (basic), Power BI, Tableau\n\ne Soft Skills: Leadership, Event Management, Public Speaking, Time Management\n\nPROJECTS\n\ne AlI-Powered Chatbot System for Automated Resume Screening and Feedback (Artificial Intelligence, NLP,\nAutomation): Developed an Al-powered chatbot to automate resume screening and candidate feedback as part of an\nacademic project. Implemented NLP techniques to extract skills, experience, and keywords from resumes and matched them\nagainst job requirements. Generated automated feedback highlighting candidate strengths and missing skill areas to reduce\nmanual screening effort. Tech: Python, NLP, Streamlit, SQL\n\ne CareerForge \u2014 Resume Builder Web Application (Web Development, Frontend, React): Built a responsive\nweb-based resume builder with real-time preview functionality. Implemented reusable React components, dynamic form\nhandling, and section-wise resume generation. Focused on clean UI design, usability, and client-side data validation. Tech:\nReact.js, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, Chakra UI\n\ne Marks Analyzer and Course Recommendation System (Web Development, Database Systems): Developed a\nweb application to analyze student academic performance using structured marks data. Designed relational database schemas\nand implemented SQL queries for efficient data storage and retrieval. Built rule-based logic to recommend suitable courses\nbased on students\u2019 performance trends. Tech: HTML, CSS, JavaScript, MySQL\n\ne Multiple Disease Prediction System (Machine Learning, Data Science): Built machine learning models to predict\ndiabetes, heart disease, and Parkinson\u2019s disease using clinical datasets. Applied Logistic Regression and Support Vector\nMachines (SVM) for classification tasks. Performed data preprocessing, feature selection, and model evaluation using accuracy\nmetrics. Tech: Python, Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-learn, Streamlit\n\nVOLUNTEER EXPERIENCE\n\nVice President - ACADS (CSE AIML Student Association) Kolhapur, India\ne Led a team of 50+ members to organize technical and career-focused events for AIML students.\n\ne Increased participation in the flagship \u201cBeyond Resume\u201d event from 180 to 400 registrations.\n\ne Coordinated with faculty, speakers, and student teams for smooth event execution.\n\nEntrepreneurship Cell Representative (ECR) \u2014 E-Cell Kolhapur, India\ne Selected as an E-Cell representative during the first year.\n\ne Assisted in organizing entrepreneurship-focused events and student activities.\n\ne Collaborated with core team members for event coordination and student outreach.", "embedding": [-0.10004550218582153, -0.0014373210724443197, -0.0070683215744793415, 0.015143861062824726, -0.022339768707752228, -0.07619554549455643, 0.015289640985429287, 0.08103086799383163, -0.09136436134576797, 0.0016088425181806087, -0.011961342766880989, -0.08546307682991028, 0.05699854716658592, -0.013486083596944809, 0.010115434415638447, 0.030890347436070442, 0.040137890726327896, -0.05364636704325676, -0.016048841178417206, -0.07197200506925583, 0.007996991276741028, 0.08279299736022949, 0.08591777086257935, -0.08006034046411514, 0.01400336530059